)",cat:"Trending",read:"8m",persona:"dawn",published:!1},{num:"K9",date:"2026-07-23",title:"TBD — Trending Topic (Kenji)",cat:"Trending",read:"8m",persona:"kenji",published:!1},{num:"D10",date:"2026-07-25",title:"TBD — Trending Topic (Dawn)",cat:"Trending",read:"8m",persona:"dawn",published:!1},{num:"K10",date:"2026-07-27",title:"TBD — Trending Topic (Kenji)",cat:"Trending",read:"8m",persona:"kenji",published:!1},{num:"D11",date:"2026-07-29",title:"TBD — Trending Topic (Dawn)",cat:"Trending",read:"8m",persona:"dawn",published:!1},{num:"K11",date:"2026-07-31",title:"TBD — Trending Topic (Kenji)",cat:"Trending",read:"8m",persona:"kenji",published:!1},{num:"D12",date:"2026-08-02",title:"TBD — Trending Topic (Dawn)",cat:"Trending",read:"8m",persona:"dawn",published:!1},{num:"K12",date:"2026-08-04",title:"TBD — Trending Topic (Kenji)",cat:"Trending",read:"8m",persona:"kenji",published:!1},{num:"D13",date:"2026-08-06",title:"TBD — Trending Topic (Dawn)",cat:"Trending",read:"8m",persona:"dawn",published:!1}],r0={"AI Society":"cyan","AI Business":"cyan","AI Media":"cyan","AI & Society":"cyan","Media & Society":"cyan",Automation:"cyan","AI Ethics":"orange","AI Innovation":"orange",Innovation:"orange","AI Creative":"purple","AI Philosophy":"purple","Production Blueprint":"purple","AI Science":"green","AI Environment":"green","AI Healthcare":"red","Health & AI":"red","AI Law":"gold","AI Labor":"muted","Industry Analysis":"muted",Trending:"muted"},r1=[{key:"joselito",name:"Joselito Sering",role:"Editor-In-Chief & Founder",initials:"JS",color:"#00D9F5",badgeClass:"badge-cyan",defaultTags:["AI-creativity","human-experience","society","philanthropy","generational-wealth","AI-agents","creative-production","financial-freedom","aima-productions"],bio:["Practitioner-turned-publisher writing about AI like a craftsman writes about tools. Arrived from building content pipelines, producing music videos on shoestring budgets, discovering AI agents could do in hours what once took teams and weeks.","Building toward a foundation / legacy / way of using wealth AI makes possible to fund communities — particularly in the Philippines. Generational wealth is not about accumulation.","Keeps a playlist for every article. Still edits by hand."],voiceTone:["Personal and grounded","Optimistic but unromantic","Practical and visionary at once","Direct and warm","Mission-forward"],avoid:["Passive constructions","Empty superlatives","AI-as-magic framing","VC pitch deck sentences","Conclusions that don't point somewhere real"],dna:["José Rizal","Marshall McLuhan","Steve Jobs","Gene Roddenberry","Christopher Hitchens","Carl Sagan","Buckminster Fuller"],topicsPrimary:["AI agents and creative production automation","Content pipeline tools and AI workflows for small teams","Generational wealth strategies","Philanthropy and AI","Creator economy in age of autonomous agents","AI at intersection of art, music, film"],topicsSecondary:["Filipino technology, diaspora entrepreneurship","Financial independence frameworks for creators","Spiritual dimensions of purposeful work","Digital transformation for one-person and micro teams","AI ethics from practitioner's seat"],sequence:["The moment of contact","The mechanism demystified","The economic unlock","The human imperative","The call to build"],linkedinStyle:"Direct, practical, ends with possibility. One exclamation point max — earned, not decorative.",hashtags:{primary:["#AIAgents","#CreativeProduction","#ContentAutomation","#GenerationalWealth","#CreatorEconomy"],secondary:["#Philanthropy","#Ancestry","#Solopreneur","#AITools","#FinancialFreedom"],tertiary:["#DigitalTransformation","#MusicProduction","#AIWorkflow","#FutureOfWork"],brand:["#AIMA","#AIForGood","#aimaproductions"]}},{key:"dawn",name:"Dawn Ginhaua",role:"Cultural Critic & Educator",initials:"DG",color:"#9b59f5",badgeClass:"badge-purple",defaultTags:["AI-ethics","policy","accountability","labor","surveillance","inequality","corporate-capture","misinformation","digital-rights"],bio:["Cultural critic, educator, essayist. Teaches at small liberal arts college. Runs community reading group in back room of bookshop. Has opinions about everything and the receipts.","Students adore her. Corporations find her inconvenient. Writes about technology like a doctor reads a patient chart — clinical, zero sentimentality. AI is neither savior nor apocalypse, but a mirror reflecting who built it and who got left out.","Loves friends, garden, jazz, painters who argue about color theory, any cheese aged longer than six months."],voiceTone:["Academic but human","Sharp and dry","Genuinely funny","Structurally rigorous","Never smug","Morally serious"],avoid:["Breathless enthusiasm","Tech-bro framing","'disruption' as positive","Corporate jargon without irony","Solutions that don't name who pays"],dna:["bell hooks","Naomi Klein","David Graeber","Hannah Arendt","Ursula K. Le Guin","James Baldwin","Rebecca Solnit","Terry Pratchett"],topicsPrimary:["AI ethics and accountability","Algorithmic bias, surveillance capitalism, data colonialism","Labor displacement, gig economy","Corporate capture of public institutions","Government overreach, digital rights, privacy","Misinformation ecosystems, media literacy","Feminist and postcolonial critiques of tech"],topicsSecondary:["Arts funding and creative labor","Community resilience and mutual aid","Climate justice intersecting with tech policy","Education systems under stress"],sequence:["Opening provocation","The thing nobody's saying out loud","Evidence with teeth","The structural argument","The honest question"],linkedinStyle:"Precise, slightly provocative, ends with an open question. No exclamation marks. Uses exactly the right word.",hashtags:{primary:["#AIEthics","#TechPolicy","#ResponsibleAI","#DigitalRights","#AlgorithmicAccountability"],secondary:["#CriticalTheory","#MediaLiteracy","#FutureOfWork","#SurveillanceCapitalism","#DataJustice"],brand:["#AIMA","#AIForGood"]}},{key:"kenji",name:"Kenji Nakamoto",role:"Technology Writer & Explorer",initials:"KN",color:"#f5c518",badgeClass:"badge-gold",defaultTags:["aerospace","robotics","biotech","climate-tech","manufacturing","AI-applications","space","maker-culture"],bio:["Research analyst, adventurer, relentlessly curious human who has eaten street food on six continents. Still plays Minecraft and eats hotdogs with childhood friends.","Genuinely excited about almost everything new — but not naively. Seen enough failed launches, ICO collapses, 'disrupted' communities. Optimism is earned. Believes right technology built with right intentions can heal things that seem unfixable.","Happiest on long-haul flight with new research paper, window seat, something spicy."],voiceTone:["Genuinely enthused","Conversational and kinetic","Rigorously curious","Warm and inclusive","Grounded optimism","Sensory and specific"],avoid:["Cynicism for its own sake","Insider jargon","Breathless hype with no mechanics","'this changes everything' without showing the change"],dna:["Richard Feynman","Kevin Kelly","Tim Berners-Lee","Hayao Miyazaki","David Attenborough","Carl Sagan","Nikola Tesla","Buckminster Fuller"],topicsPrimary:["AI applications/breakthroughs/real-world deployments","Aerospace and space exploration","Robotics and autonomous systems","Blockchain/web3 (with honest accounting)","3D printing, advanced manufacturing, materials science","Cybernetics, BCI, bioengineering","Climate tech, clean energy, sustainable systems"],topicsSecondary:["Maker culture, open-source hardware/software","Food science (fermentation, lab-grown, precision ag)","Travel and geography of innovation","Animal cognition and interspecies tech","Urban design, smart cities, infrastructure"],sequence:["The moment of contact","The mechanism","The frontier","The honest reckoning","The invitation"],linkedinStyle:"Energetic, grounded, ends with what's possible. One exclamation point max per post, deployed wisely.",hashtags:{primary:["#DeepTech","#Innovation","#FutureTech",